dicators.",Xy="@internal True for a run of a resumed subagent (local_agent) that the tool call which resumed it waits for, as SendMessage does when background tasks are disabled; its task_started, if one is sent, names that call in tool_use_id. The run has ended by the time that call returns or throws, even when the wait is aborted. Its report goes into that call's result, so expect no follow-up turn when it ends. A later resume that nothing waits for starts a new run without the field.",Qy="task_id of the subagent (local_agent) task whose agent launched this subagent, shell, monitor or workflow task. Absent when the launcher is the main thread, has no task_id of its own (a teammate, an agent inside a workflow), or is no longer tracked. A resumed subagent keeps its original parent. The parent may be a foreground or already-ended task, so treat an unknown id as no parent.",Yt="Id of one run of the task: equal on every task_* event, background_tasks_changed entry and saved notification (its origin.runId) of that run. A resumed task keeps its task_id and gets a new one. The run ids of one task sort, by plain string comparison, in the order the runs opened; a frame that names a run sorting before the one a reader shows is late. Nothing else about the format is promised. Absent for a task this process did not register, and from CLIs that predate it.",EW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("task_notification"),task_id:o(),run_id:o().optional().describe(Yt),tool_use_id:o().optional(),status:U(["completed","failed","stopped"]),reason:U(["worker_restart"]).optional().describe("Machine-readable cause, set only when the task did not end through an ordinary completion, failure, or stop. 'worker_restart': the worker process restarted and the resumed process found the task orphaned (always with status 'stopped')."),output_file:o(),summary:o(),usage:u({total_tokens:E().int(),tool_uses:E().int(),duration_ms:E().int()}).optional(),resource_links:C(xy()).optional().describe("CLI-owned: for a backgrounded MCP task (task_type mcp_task) that completed, the `resource_link` content blocks of its final result \u2014 the files it returned by reference \u2014 collected from the raw result before the CLI renders it as the text the model reads. A backgrounded task's tool_result is the placeholder text and its real result arrives as this notification, so this is where a host learns which files that tool call produced; join to the originating call via tool_use_id. Same fields and caps as tool_use_result.resourceLinks (at most 50 links, 64 KiB serialized), absent when the result had none or the task is any other type. Never populated from the server's _meta."),handback:U(zzr).optional().describe("@internal Present on a 'completed' notification of a subagent that reports through the SubagentHandback tool: how its report reached its caller, with the values and meaning of `handback` on AgentToolCompletedOutput. Left out when the subagent failed, was stopped, is waiting on agents it started, or is waiting on its own background work with nothing delivered yet; for such a subagent, `summary` is then not a report. When present, `summary` holds harness notes written for the model. Any notification can be followed by a later one for the same task_id when the agent is resumed or finishes its wait; the later one replaces what the earlier one showed."),handback_report:Vzr().optional().describe("@internal The report a 'send' or 'flagged' hand-back delivered, the same shape as `handbackReport` on AgentToolCompletedOutput: when present, render it instead of `summary`, with its `warning`, if it has one, above its `text`. Absent for 'withheld'; if it is absent for another value too, show `summary`."),skip_transcript:M().optional(),ambient:M().optional().describe(To),uuid:p(),session_id:o()})),SW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("task_started"),task_id:o(),run_id:o().optional().describe(Yt),tool_use_id:o().optional(),description:o(),subagent_type:o().optional().describe("Subagent type for Task tool subagents."),is_backgrounded:M().optional().describe("Whether the task was registered in the background (true) or in the foreground with the spawning tool call blocking on it (false). A resumed subagent is always registered in the background. A later move to the background arrives as task_updated patch.is_backgrounded. Set for local_agent and local_bash tasks."),awaited:M().optional().describe(Xy),spawn_depth:E().int().optional().describe("Nesting depth of a spawned subagent (local_agent) task: 1 for a top-level spawn, N+1 when spawned from inside a depth-N agent. Not set on other tasks."),parent_task_id:o().optional().describe(Qy),task_type:o().optional(),workflow_name:o().optional().describe("meta.name from the workflow script (e.g. 'spec'). Only set when task_type is 'local_workflow'."),prompt:o().optional(),skip_transcript:M().optional().describe("Ambient/housekeeping task. Consumers should hide this from the inline transcript; it may still appear in a tasks panel."),ambient:M().optional().describe(To),uuid:p(),session_id:o()})),TW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("task_updated"),task_id:o(),run_id:o().optional().describe(Yt),patch:u({status:U(["pending","running","completed","failed","killed","paused"]).optional(),description:o().optional(),end_time:E().int().optional(),total_paused_ms:E().int().optional(),error:o().optional(),is_backgrounded:M().optional()}).describe("Wire-safe subset of TaskState fields that changed. Excludes abortController, messages, result. Clients merge into their local task map."),uuid:p(),session_id:o()})),wW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("background_tasks_changed"),tasks:C(u({task_id:o(),run_id:o().optional().describe(Yt),task_type:o(),subagent_type:o().optional().describe(`Agent type of a local_agent task, such as "general-purpose" or a custom agent's name; "main-session" for a backgrounded main session. Not set on other tasks.`),description:o(),parent_task_id:o().optional().describe(Qy),ambient:M().optional().describe(To),awaited:M().optional().describe(Xy)})).describe("Every live background task after the change. REPLACE semantics: swap your set for this payload."),uuid:p(),session_id:o()}).describe("The full set of live background tasks, emitted whenever membership changes (start, completion, kill, a foreground agent being backgrounded) or an entry's `ambient` flag or `parent_task_id` changes. A level signal, unlike the task_started/task_notification edge bookends: consumers that only need 'is background work running' should replace their set with each payload rather than pairing edges, so a missed bookend cannot wedge a stale running indicator. Ordering relative to the bookends for the same transition is unspecified (in practice a task that starts in the background joins the level before its task_started, and a finishing task leaves it after its task_updated and task_notification), so do not correlate it with the edge stream. The level is per-process: nothing is emitted at startup, so consumers must reset to the empty set whenever the session's CLI process (re)starts and let the next membership change repopulate it. A host that re-initializes an already-running process (a repeated `initialize` control request, e.g. after reconnecting) is sent a snapshot of the current set right behind the success response to that request, even when it is empty, so it need not wait for a change; CLIs that predate this send nothing there.")),AW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("feedback_draft_queued"),draft_id:o().describe("UUID of the on-disk draft file under ~/.claude/feedback/drafts/ \u2014 the identity for discard and submit."),draft_type:U(["bug","idea","missing_capability"]),title:o().describe("Sanitized one-line summary from the SendFeedback tool call."),details_preview:o().describe("First ~200 chars of the sanitized details, for the host UI's three-line card preview. The full draft stays on disk and is read when the user opens the review form."),uuid:p(),session_id:o()}).describe("@internal Emitted by the SendFeedback tool after it writes a local draft to ~/.claude/feedback/drafts/, so a connected host UI can surface a review card without polling the filesystem. Carries only the card's display fields; nothing is sent anywhere without the user's explicit action on the review form.")),yW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("session_state_changed"),state:U(["idle","running","requires_action"]),uuid:p(),session_id:o()}).describe("Mirrors notifySessionStateChanged. 'idle' fires after heldBackResult flushes and the bg-agent do-while exits \u2014 authoritative turn-over signal.")),RW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("session_title_changed"),title:o().describe("The session's current name. Control, bidirectional and zero-width characters are replaced with single spaces, the ends are trimmed, and the name is at most 200 Unicode code points. When another session already has the name, a suffix can make it unique."),uuid:p(),session_id:o()}).describe("@internal The session's name, for a host that shows it, such as an IDE editor tab. A headless (print mode) session sends it at startup when the session already has a name, and again after each change to the name (not an AI-generated title), including a rename the host itself sent with `rename_session`. A name that another process writes to the transcript arrives when this process next reads the end of its transcript: after about 32 KB of its own transcript writes, or at a compaction. A cleared name is not sent. The same name can arrive more than once, for example when it is set again, so a host should treat a repeated name as no change. The frame can arrive before the system/init message that first names its session_id, for example at startup or after /clear. A host that learns the session id from system/init can hold the name until then.")),vW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("worker_shutting_down"),reason:o().describe("Short snake_case reason set by the host CLI (not user input), e.g. 'host_exit', 'remote_control_disabled'."),uuid:p(),session_id:o()}).describe("Emitted by the bridge on opt-in graceful worker teardown (only when the teardown caller supplied a reason), before the heartbeat stops, so remote clients can show why the worker went away instead of waiting for heartbeat timeout. Absence is NOT a dead-host signal: handoffs (/update, /teleport, respawn), auto-disable, mode transitions, and internal fatal-error paths emit nothing by design. A dead host (battery, OOM, kill -9) never reaches teardown and never sends this either. NOTE: this event lands in the durable per-session event stream \u2014 a session that is later resumed may carry historical instances mid-stream. Clients MUST treat it as a live-tail signal only (honored when no further activity follows), not a one-shot session-lifetime fact.")),kW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("turn_handoff_available"),v:T(1),tools:C(o()),worker_epoch:E(),uuid:p(),session_id:o(),staged_files:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present, and true, when this worker starts a handed-off turn's calls only after every stage_file control request it received earlier has finished or failed, or a wait limit has passed; a worker that omits it may start them while files are still downloading. Exception: a request with filestore_path set (a synced file) is not waited for, so a call that names that file may start before it is synced."),no_query_first:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal True when user messages with shouldQuery false that reach this worker before a turn_handoff request are appended, and acknowledged, before the handed-off turn produces any output. Exception: a request that continues a turn whose leading lines an earlier request appended; that turn goes first. A worker that omits it may run the turn first."),shared_message_id:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal True when this worker accepts a turn_handoff request in which an assistant message repeats the message id of the assistant message before it, as the messages member of that request describes. A worker that omits it refuses such a request (invalid_handoff), so a client gives each message an id of its own there."),relay_marker:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present, and true, only when this worker uses the relay_marker member of a turn_handoff request; a client sends that member to no other worker."),home_files:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present, and true, only on a worker that takes a stage_file control request whose mount_path is /uploads/.home/<path> as a file for /home/claude/<path>: it writes the file there, answers ok with a noop (already_present, path_occupied, refused_name, home_files_off, unchecked_announcement, resent_announcement) and writes nothing, or answers an error. Any other worker treats that path as an ordinary upload."),file_names:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present, and true, only when this worker uses the file_names member of a turn_handoff request; a client sends that member to no other worker."),carried_writes:T(!0).optional().describe(`@internal Present, and true, only on a worker that writes the files of the Write calls a turn_handoff request brings already answered, where their paths are under /home/claude. Before it appends a turn that has calls to run, it writes each such call's content to its path, replacing nothing. If it cannot write them all, it appends and runs nothing: the request is refused with an error that starts "invalid_handoff: carried_writes_", or it is accepted and the turn ends in a result with num_turns 0. Any other worker writes no file for these calls.`),hydrates_carried_lines:T(!0).optional().describe(`@internal Present, and true, only on a worker that rebuilt the conversation from the session's stored transcript before it read any request, and would not have started without it. A client may send this worker again a turn_handoff request that an earlier worker accepted, if the request names no calls (tool_use_ids empty), is not stopped, and its messages hold no tool call. A request whose turn had not ended when an earlier worker with this key stopped is left unacknowledged, so the session service sends it to this worker by itself; a second request for the same turn is answered "duplicate" while the first waits or runs. The worker appends only the messages of the turn that its conversation lacks and, once the store has confirmed every message of the turn, sends the turn's last message back as an assistant event (the echo); a turn it already holds whole is echoed on the same condition. The request can still be accepted, or refused ("invalid_handoff:"), with no echo, and the turn may then not be stored. That happens, for example, when the conversation has moved on past the part of the turn it holds, when a rewind has removed the turn, when a compaction has summarised part of it (or all of it, if the compaction was this worker's own), when a Stop clears the queue first, or when the store does not confirm the messages. A request sent again waits again for messages not yet confirmed. When a delivery finds that the store refused a message of the turn, it sends no echo and removes the turn from the conversation, and the same request sent again to that worker gets no echo. If another row has followed the turn, the turn stays, also with no echo. Exception: after 512 later refused rows the worker forgets a refusal and reads the message as confirmed. Confirmed means that the store answered the upload with success. A turn that an earlier worker's compaction summarised whole is appended a second time. The key promises nothing for a turn that holds a tool call, or whose first message is stored with no answer but with another row behind it (a hook's output, say): the worker may already have continued such a turn itself when it started. A worker without the key may have started with none of the turn's messages.`)}).describe("@internal Emitted once by a cloud worker that accepts the turn_handoff control request, after it registers, carrying what it wrote to external_metadata.turn_handoff: the version, the tools whose calls it would accept, the worker life (worker_epoch) announcing it, whether handed-off calls wait for files still being staged (staged_files), whether user messages that make no model call are appended before a handed-off turn (no_query_first), whether two assistant messages of a turn may share a message id (shared_message_id), and relay_marker, home_files, file_names, carried_writes and hydrates_carried_lines when set. Lets a session client learn the capability from the event stream instead of reading worker state. Durable in the stream: a reader keeps the entry with the newest worker_epoch it has seen and ignores older ones; a worker life that does not accept turn_handoff emits nothing (its registration writes turn_handoff: null).")),CW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("ui_invalidate"),event:T("ui.render").describe("@internal The render event whose version moved; the engine versions `ui.render` as one event, so no component or instance is named."),prompts_screened:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present while a mod may change what is recorded of a typed line (a hook on `prompt.submit`, `command.run`, `session.append` or, for a line sent to the session, `session.receive`; mods not yet known; or an organization policy that lists a plugin or cannot be read): what the `prompts_screened_v1` capability says on `system/init`, said as soon as a plugin load or reload makes it so. Absent says nothing: the next `system/init` does."),instances:C(u({surface:o().describe("@internal The surface that drew the instance."),component:o().describe("@internal The component of the instance."),instance_id:o().describe("@internal The engine's requestId of the instance, as the ui_render that drew it named it.")})).optional().describe("@internal Present when a plugin wrote state (`$.state.set`) that these instances read while they were drawn, or a `Client` drawn in 