ed (CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT), alias_1m_unsupported, blocked_by_hook (also when the model kept changing while the hooks ran, which a retry may get past), check_failed (the API settled nothing about the model; a retry may pass), check_rejected (the API answered with an error no retry or sign-in clears), credits_required (a 429 whose body carries that error_code, and nothing clears it by itself), rate_limit (any other 429, even a usage-credits refusal that has no such code or that clears by itself), auth_failed (sign in again), model_not_current, verdict_pending (not a refusal: the outcome follows as a system/informational message), internal_error (the switch may or may not have applied). apply_flag_settings: verdict_pending, rarely internal_error. set_permission_mode: invalid_mode, bypass_restricted, bypass_disabled, bypass_not_launched, and for auto auto_mode_settings, auto_mode_circuit_breaker, auto_mode_fast_mode, auto_mode_model or auto_mode_unavailable. remote_control (a failed enable whose cause the bridge reported): remote_control_auth (sign in again), remote_control_terminal, remote_control_ended_elsewhere, remote_control_policy_disabled. get_workspace_diff: workspace_diff_pending (the diff was not ready when the reply was due; ask again shortly, since a diff that finishes in the meantime is returned to the next request that comes within a minute). interrupt (a claude-code-server tenant, by worker_epoch): stale_worker_epoch (it is for another worker life; no turn was stopped), invalid_worker_epoch (it is no whole number of 1 or more; likewise). read_file with the anchor as_written: read_denied (the one refusal, the same for every cause; a plain read_file and the other anchors carry no code). Absent on every other error; new values are additive, so treat an unknown one as absent."),model:o().optional().describe("@internal set_model only: the model the session's next turn runs as of this answer, spelled as on the success payload's `model`. A refusal leaves the model as it was, and a restarted cloud worker can already run the requested model: it starts on the host's last pick. One refusal moves it: when the server refuses for good the model that a restarted worker started on, before any turn, the session goes back to the model recorded for it. The fixed 'set_model failed' reply can follow an applied switch, so it names the model too. A refusal fallback in a running turn, before or after this answer, can move the next turn to another model. `claude -p` writes it on its stream-json control channel, unless it cannot read the model. A claude-code-server tenant writes it too, except on its 'still pending' answer. claude -p's Remote Control bridge lane and interactive Remote Control leave it out."),pending_permission_requests:AR(),pending_user_dialog_requests:yR()}).describe("The request failed or was rejected (unknown subtype, invalid arguments, or an error while handling it).")),Xzr=f(()=>u({type:T("control_response"),response:Ue([V1(),j1()])}).describe("Envelope for the single reply to a control_request, sent by whichever side received the request.")),Y2t=f(()=>u({type:T("control_cancel_request"),request_id:o().describe("The request_id of the control_request being withdrawn.")}).describe("Tells the other side that the sender no longer needs the answer to one of its own in-flight control_requests (for example a pending can_use_tool prompt after the turn was interrupted, or one that another client already answered). Either side may send it for a request it originated. The sender stops waiting at once and ignores any control_response that still arrives for that request_id; a receiver that can abort the work does so and may still reply (typically with an error), otherwise it simply completes the request. There is no reply to the cancel itself.")),RR=f(()=>u({type:T("keep_alive")}).describe("Liveness heartbeat. Either side may send it at any time (the CLI emits it periodically, for example while a long-running control reques